# .api-pending — operations that are BUILT but not RELEASED.
#
# scripts/check-api.sh normally fails any `op` fact production does not serve,
# because shipping one means a command that 404s for every customer. An entry
# here says "we know, this is deliberate, it is verified against a local or
# staging server and is waiting on the API deploy".
#
# Rules:
#   * scripts/release.sh REFUSES while this file has any entry. That is the
#     real gate — the tree may be ahead, a release may not.
#   * an entry only counts while production genuinely lacks the operation.
#     Listing one that has shipped is an error, not a leftover.
#
# Format: one verbatim `METHOD /path` line, ids written as {id}.

# 2026-08-04 — Phase 4 (C2). Verified against a local API v3 server on :8890
# (218 operations, branch `staging`): new -> finished -> in_progress observed
# end to end. Production served 182 operations and 404s both of these.
POST /api/v3/tasks/{id}/complete
POST /api/v3/tasks/{id}/reopen
